    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0052" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg46"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith a translation of a telegram received from Chang Chih-tung, viceroy at
                    Wu-chang, relating to the execution of the provincial treasurer of Chih-li and
                    other officials at Pao-ting Fu, together with my reply sent him through our
                    consul at Hankou.</p>
                <p>The opinion of the viceroy that these punishments should have been inflicted by
                    the Chinese authorities agrees, I believe, with the views of the Department as
                    shown by the Department’s note of September 21 to the German chargé d’affaires
                    in Washington.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d50-a1.xml" xpointer="d50-a1"/>
            </div>
